> Original four taxa and five characters

Retain the original leaf-state columns0011,0011,1100,0100,0001 across taxa
A,B,C,D. The native helpers build the same seven-node layouts and complete
columns with ignored internal entries. Compare the three unrooted quartet
topologies using balanced rooted representatives AB|CD, AC|BD, AD|BC. This is
the complete set of unrooted binary four-taxon splits, not a claim that there
are only three rooted four-taxon binary trees.

Independent characters add their actual minimum scores, with equal unit change
costs and no branch-length weighting. The report compares these three prescribed
candidates; the library’s scorer does not implement a general maximum-parsimony
topology search. The artificial columns are the original hand-checkable fixture,
not a claimed empirical DNA alignment.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/parsimony_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/maximum_parsimony.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto cols = dm::algorithms::parsimony_demo_columns();
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"AB/CD", "AC/BD", "AD/BC"};
    std::vector<dm::algorithms::ParsimonyTree> trees{dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_tree(0, 1, 2, 3),
                                                     dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_tree(0, 2, 1, 3),
                                                     dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_tree(0, 3, 1, 2)};
    std::vector<double> totals;
    std::print("| prescribed quartet | site0 | site1 | site2 | site3 | site4 | actual total |\n| --- | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < trees.size(); ++i) {
        auto scores = dm::algorithms::parsimony_site_scores(trees[i], cols);
        auto total = dm::algorithms::parsimony_score(trees[i], cols);
        totals.push_back(total);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   scores[0], scores[1], scores[2], scores[3], scores[4], total);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(totals, labels, "actual changes");
    p.x_label("prescribed unrooted quartet representative").y_label(
        "actual summed minimum unit changes").title("Original four taxa: actual five-character scores").save_svg("build/parsimony_original.svg");
}
```
