> Trace an actual ancestral assignment

The first original character gives A=B=0 and C=D=1. Read the actual masks and
chosen states from one native run on AB|CD. The tree diagram displays each
actual chosen state; the edge table distinguishes exact equal/unequal choices.
Every observed leaf is retained, and the counted edge changes attain the
computed lower bound.

Ancestral states remain ambiguous when masks have multiple bits. The
smallest-bit tie rule is an explicit reproducibility convention, not biological
evidence for the smaller numeric label. Relabelling states preserves scores,
while this tie convention can select a correspondingly different representative
optimum.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/parsimony_witness.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/maximum_parsimony.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto tree = dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_tree(0, 1, 2, 3);
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::fitch_trace(tree,
                                    dm::algorithms::parsimony_demo_columns().front());
    std::print("| actual parent | actual child | chosen parent state | chosen child state | actual changed " "edge |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &e : t.edges)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.parent, e.child,
                   e.parent_state, e.child_state, e.changed);
    std::array<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint, 7> positions{{{0, 0}, {6, 0},
                                                         {12, 0}, {18, 0},
                                                         {3, 4}, {15, 4}, {9, 8}}};
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < positions.size(); ++i)
        d.node(std::to_string(i), positions[i],
               std::format("Actual node {}\nstate {}, mask {}", i,
                           t.analysis.states[i], t.analysis.masks[i]));
    for (auto &e : t.edges)
        d.edge(std::to_string(e.parent), std::to_string(e.child));
    d.save_svg("build/parsimony_witness.svg");
}
```
