> Checked trees, exact masks and work

The input is a rooted full binary tree: leaves have exact marker(−1,−1); every
internal node has two distinct valid children; the root has no parent; every
other node has exactly one; every supplied node is reachable. Validate all
fields before indexing or shifting, including malformed disconnected components.
An empty tree is root−1 with no nodes and an empty state vector. Each nonempty
column has exactly N node-indexed entries; internal values are ignored, but
every leaf state must be0..31. State31 uses a defined unsigned32-bit shift,
avoiding the old unchecked invalid-shift path.

Both passes are iterative. Validation, postorder scoring and top-down witness
assignment take O(N) time and O(N) returned/working storage. For C characters,
complete tree/all-column validation precedes any evaluation, and scoring takes
O(N(C+1)) time with reusable structural order. Summed int scores reject
overflow. This is unordered unit-cost parsimony, not a likelihood model,
weighted Sankoff recurrence or a general optimizer over tree space.

Complete capture admits7N logical entries for N>0, or one for an empty tree:
root, two child-id scalars per node, input states, actual masks/chosen states,
node-step records and N−1 edge records. Default limit is one million; zero
disables only that optional cap. Fields, vector headers, capacities, runtime
traversal state and bytes are excluded. Validation and admission precede
copying/evaluation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/parsimony_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/maximum_parsimony.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto tree = dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_tree(0, 1, 2, 3);
    std::vector<std::array<int, 4>> patterns{{0, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 1, 1},
                                             {0, 1, 2, 3}, {0, 0, 0, 1},
                                             {0, 31, 0, 31}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels{"constant", "split", "four states",
                                    "singleton", "high bit"};
    std::vector<double> scores;
    std::print("| prescribed character | actual score | actual nodes | actual unions | actual witness " "changes | capture entries |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < patterns.size(); ++i) {
        auto t =
            dm::algorithms::fitch_trace(tree,
                                        dm::algorithms::parsimony_four_taxon_column(patterns[i]));
        scores.push_back(t.analysis.score);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   t.analysis.score, t.analysis.work.nodes,
                   t.analysis.work.unions, t.analysis.work.changes,
                   t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(scores, labels, "actual changes");
    p.x_label("prescribed four-leaf character").y_label("actual minimum unit changes").title("Fixed AB|CD tree: actual character controls").save_svg("build/parsimony_controls.svg");
}
```
