\alttext(Constant, split, four-state, singleton and state31 controls use the same checked producer.)

> Verification and references

Native tests exhaust81 three-state four-taxon columns on all three quartet
representatives and enumerate every one of27 internal-state assignments
independently. They compare exact minimum scores/root masks, actual postorder
reads/writes, every chosen witness edge, operation counts and complete quotas.
Original five-site scores5/8/8, safe state31, empty trees, malformed complete
structures/columns, ignored internal values and ownership are covered.
A100001-node highly skewed full binary tree checks iterative execution. The
shared ten-report batch passes 71 CTest cases, 29 directly instrumented
ASan/UBSan cases, 130 compiled and executed public examples, 598/598 scoped
documentation definitions and ten representative hovers. Independent Python
arbitrary-precision, hashlib, sorted-window, RNG, polynomial, graph and
full-assignment references verify 224,229 actual records. Frozen comparisons
preserve ordinary legacy outputs, including selected clique identities, original
density graphs and memetic partitions. Twelve checkout headers and twelve
identically installed headers compile independently; an installed-header native
consumer links and runs. All four complete programs and all four native figures
pass execution and visual review, and HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed
results and identical image bytes. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-224-233/`.

Fitch (1971), *Toward Defining the Course of Evolution: Minimum Change for a
Specific Tree Topology*, Systematic Zoology20(4),406–416,
[doi:10.2307/2412116|https://doi.org/10.2307/2412116]. The implemented objective
and fixed-topology limitation are explicit above.

The
[original Fitch paper scan|https://evoluscope.fr/phylographe/biblio/Fitch1971.pdf]
retains the fixed-topology problem statement and intersection/union
construction.
